# {{project_name}}

A CHAP-compatible disease forecasting model created with chap-python-sdk.

## Installation

```bash
# Install with uv (recommended)
uv sync

# Or with pip
pip install -e ".[dev]"
```

## Usage

### CLI

Train and predict using the command-line interface:

```bash
# Train model
uv run {{project_name}} train-cmd train_data.csv model.pkl

# Generate predictions
uv run {{project_name}} predict-cmd model.pkl historic.csv future.csv predictions.csv

# Or use directly with python -m
uv run python -m {{project_name_underscore}}.cli train-cmd train_data.csv model.pkl
```

### Python API

```python
import pandas as pd
from {{project_name_underscore}}.model import train, predict, {{project_name_class}}Config

# Prepare training data
train_data = pd.DataFrame({
    "time_period": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5],
    "location": ["A", "A", "A", "A", "A"],
    "disease_cases": [10, 15, 12, 18, 20],
})

# Train model
config = {{project_name_class}}Config(n_samples=100)
model = train(config, train_data)

# Generate predictions
future_data = pd.DataFrame({
    "time_period": [6, 7],
    "location": ["A", "A"],
})
historic_data = train_data  # Recent history for context

predictions = predict(config, model, historic_data, future_data)
print(predictions)
```

### CHAP Integration

This model can be used with CHAP via the `MLproject` file:

```bash
chap evaluate --model-name /path/to/{{project_name}} --dataset-name ISIMIP_dengue_harmonized
```

